WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.468
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.869
to the attic crawl space.

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:07.073
We have been focussing a lot
on the tiny door back there,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.276
as well as the various
miniseries books

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:13.012
mysteriously appearing
over here on the side table.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:16.349
And I just wanna say
I am really hoping a copy

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.550
of the "John Adams" biography

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.018
that inspired
the "John Adams" miniseries,

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.319
starring Paul Giamatti,
will show up,

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:23.523
but, with an infestation
of miniseries books like this,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.358
you don't get
to choose the titles.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:26.559
They just show up.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.360
Anyway, speaking
of presidents --

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.931
classic segue --
President Trump seems intent

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.300
on opening the economy
by the end of the month,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.602
even though he doesn't have
the power to do that

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.105
and public health experts
have warned against it.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.074
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:44.944
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.380
Since before Trump
was even considered

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.948
a serious candidate
for president,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.951
it's always been clear that
he's worshipped authoritarians

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.219
and sought to emulate them.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.354
For one thing,
those are the world leaders

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.589
he gets along with best.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.092
For example, he's repeatedly
heaped praise

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.994
on Chinese President Xi Jinping,

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.429
including during the
coronavirus outbreak.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:04.664
Trump tweeted...

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.710
Trump wants us
to forget all that now

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.813
because he thinks our brains
are like his, but they're not.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.315
Most of us can form
and retain memories,

00:01:23.315 --> 00:01:26.652
while Trump has the memory
of a goldfish who smokes weed.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.121
"Hey, man, has that --

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:32.524
has that treasure chest
always been there?"

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.060
And, by the way,
I know it's hard

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.895
to remember back further
than a day,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.430
since every day is a year
and every year is a month

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.733
and every month is
February-March-Augus-tember,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.135
but Trump has claimed many times

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:44.670
that Article 2
of the Constitution,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.173
which outlines the powers
of the presidency,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.076
allows him to do literally
whatever he wants,

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:52.278
even though
it obviously does not.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.280
-Then I have an Article 2,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.082
where I have the right to do
whatever I want,

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.150
as president, but,

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.219
I don't even talk about that.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.687
-"I have an Article 2"

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.956
is how a cabbie from Queens
would say it

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.791
will fighting
with a traffic cop.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.160
[ changes accent ]
C'mon, you can't give me
a ticket for parking here!

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.464
I got an Article 2 that tells me
I can do whatever I want!

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.866
Some people were still
holding out hope

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:16.602
that, when [bleep] got serious,
Trump would get serious,

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:20.172
when, in reality, it was clear
he would just be [bleep]

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:22.475
And sure enough,
as recently as Monday,

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.510
he was insisting, once again,
that, as president,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.045
he had absolute power

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.214
and could unilaterally order
every state in the country

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.548
to lift their
stay-at-home orders

00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:32.752
and reopen their economies
as early as May 1st.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:38.624
What authority you do have?

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:39.958
-Well, I have
the ultimate authority.

00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:42.327
I have the absolute right
to do it, if I want to.

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:45.798
When somebody's the president
of the United States,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.500
the authority is total

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.667
and that's way it's gotta be.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.002
The president
of the United States

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.138
has the authority to do

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.407
what the president
has the authority to do,

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.975
which is very powerful.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.576
-Talk about a meaningless
statement --

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.712
"The president
of the United States

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.213
has the authority to do

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.915
what the president
has the authority to do."

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:06.418
It's kind of the perfect
zero-information sentence.

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:07.987
It's like sayin'...
[ As Trump ] Hey!

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.490
I gotta be me!

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.358
Yeah, okay,
but who are you, though,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.994
the wannabe dictator who's
best friends with Kim Jong-un

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.631
or the cherubic mascot for
Love Handles Golf Resort &amp; Spa?

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.799
Seriously,
if the Continental Congress

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:22.568
had actually written that
down on parchment,

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:24.170
Ben Franklin would've charged
in the room and been like,

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.339
"Guys, guy-uy-s,
c'mon, what the hell is this?

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.108
Were you drunk last night?"
And George Washington

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.910
would've been like,
"Sorry, boss.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.444
We drank too much applejack."

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:34.213
But John Adams
would've been like,

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:35.948
"I was busy defending
the soldiers

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.049
in the Boston Massacre."

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:38.483
See?

00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:39.686
[ Singsong ] You guys!

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.487
I did watch the miniseries.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.888
By the way, here's my impression

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:46.025
of Paul Giamatti
in "John Adams."

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.726
[ Grumbling ]

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:50.028
Abigail.

00:03:50.028 --> 00:03:51.830
For real,
such a good miniseries.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.099
Giamatti was so good.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:56.001
So good, Lin Manuel left
John Adams out of Hamilton."

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.202
Is my theory.

00:03:57.202 --> 00:03:59.638
And can we just agree now

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.674
that there should never,
ever, be

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.808
a Donald Trump miniseries,

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.578
or at least wait as long
as HBO did

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:08.080
after his term ended
to make "John Adams"?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.083
Just don't make an actor
of Paul Giamatti's caliber

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.117
ever say the line

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:13.452
"The president
of the United States

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:14.586
has the authority to do

00:04:14.586 --> 00:04:16.622
what the president
has the authority to do."

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.857
Because that's
an actual sentence

00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:20.026
that came out of Trump's mouth.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.161
I mean, can you imagine

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.296
if President Obama
had said something like that?

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:25.531
First of all, you can't,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.966
because Obama was a smart person

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.301
who knew more than five words.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.902
I mean, you never tuned
into a press conference

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.471 line:0%
and saw a chyron that said...

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.910 line:0%
Second, Fox News would've gone
into full meltdown mode.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.379
Sean Hannity
would've screamed so loud,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.480
the glass of your TV
woulda cracked.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.483
Sorry, your grandfather's TV.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:46.151
In fact, on his show, this week,

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:49.855
Hannity insisted states
could actually reopen sooner

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:50.856
than the end of the month.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:54.226
-I think most states can reopen

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:55.762
even sooner than later.

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:57.797
We don't have to wait
'til may 1st.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:04:59.831
-Okay, Sean.
You go first.

00:04:59.831 --> 00:05:00.900
Take your show outside

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.234
and host it in Times Square

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.003
with Buzz Lightyear and Elmo.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.104
Ask people to cough on you.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.705
You can call it
"Cough-ee [coffee] Talk."

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:09.208
And then,
after significant pushback,

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.977
President Werewolf
seemingly changed course

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.646
and claimed that he would be
consulting with governors

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:17.483
on when to open their economies
and would authorize them

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.485
